Chris Adams had the same problem with the 5.1A version of that
patch kit. He even contacted HPAQ support, to no avail. Looks
like the dependency is intentional, however braindead it is to
have a static library depend on a bunch of executables.

Both Chris Adams and Oisin McGuinness suggested that by editing
the patch ctrl file I could remove the dependency. I didn't
do this mainly because I couldn't know to what kind of trouble
it would lead down the road.

What I did was to move cups to a different location and
install OSFPRINT.

	Dirk Hufnagel

original message:

> I have a problem with the Sep-11 jumbo patchkit (SSRT2275, SSRT2229) for
> Tru64 4.0F. Patch C 00815.01 (Fix for SSRT2275, libtermcap, libtermlib)
> requieres patch C 00802.02 (Fix for SSRT2260, lpq, lpr, lprm), but I can't
> install that patch since we don't use the Tru64 printing system, we use 
> cups.
> In fact, none of the printing packages are installed and that never caused
> a problem with patch dependencies.
> 
> Because patch C 00802.02 doesn't install, other patches which requiere
> this patch don't install either, for instance the security patches
> for telnetd,csh,libcurses and dxterm. I am worried that this will cause
> problems later on, not only for security reasons, but also with other
> patch dependencies.
> 
> Is that dependency on the printing patch real or just some error made when
> the patch kit was created ? Can I force patch 00802.02 to install ?
> 
> I could see around this problem by moving cups to another location
> (right now it's in the same places the system print binaries would be),
> install the Tru64 print packages and patches and then disable lpd,
> but I would like to avoid this if possible.



