We're having a problem on a Tru64 5.1A (PK2) server, where no one is able to
login.

Existing sessions are running fine.  I can't see anything obviously wrong.
But whenever someone tries to login to the server, whether via telnet,
rlogin or ssh, the login session hangs immediately after reporting the last
successful and unsuccessful logins.

Eg.:

----------------------------------
david@zebedee:/usr/users/sydney/david > telnet bunyip                   
Trying 10.130.10.40...
Connected to bunyip.
Escape character is '^]'.


Compaq Tru64 UNIX V5.1A (Rev. 1885) (bunyip.acxiom.com.au) (pts/64)

login: david
Password:
Last   successful login for david: Wed Sep 18 15:39:22 EST 2002 from
redback.acxiom.com.au
Last unsuccessful login for david: Sun Sep  1 11:18:55 EST 2002

------------------------------

And there it hangs, not coming back.

Commands run via rsh from other servers are running ok.  ftp to the server
also works, so it doesn't appear to be an authentication problem.
The lucky users who are logged in can open new shells ok, so there is no
problem with starting a shell.


Has anyone seen this sort of behaviour?

I guess I can probably fix this Microsoft-style, with a reboot, but I want
to avoid that if possible.


Thanks,

David Meiklejohn




