Once again the list comes through!

Thanks to everyone who answered.  The answer that helped me out was from
Joe Carrico who sent me the AS400 user's guide PDF.

To get to ARC on an AS400 from the SRM:

>>> set os_type NT

then power cycle the server (wait about 20 seconds).  It will boot to
the familiar ARC console where you can "run a program".  In my case,
"a:ra200rcu" which is the software for the version of Mylex controller I
am using.  Once completed, use the SRM menu option to change the os type
back to Digital Unix and power cycle, again with a 20 second delay.
After the power cycle, you are once again at the familiar SRM prompt
where you can boot Unix as normal.

Cheers,

Ralf

