The basic original question was "why are my identical machines different?".  
The answer is that I was messing around with some system parameters that I 
shouldn't have been.  The result was that on the machines with problems way 
too little "vmemory" was available (the last line in "ulimit -a").  

I undid my changes is /etc/sysconfigtab and rebooted: all is well.

Special thanks to Joe Mario of HP/Compaq/DEC back in New Hampshire.



